From 164c534dff47b785a4d8a3eea0d2955a805f9829 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DefNotALemon <dominicalexander615@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:44:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Bytteboden marketplace and Real Estate depots (winter
 update O6)

Bytteboden, a used-gear marketplace app: engines, whole sleds, hitch
receivers, trailers, groomers and ice-fishing rods, reels and augers from
private sellers round the map. Listings come and go one at a time, each
with its own lifespan. Used gear is 65-90% condition: a little less
performance and a reusable WEAR look (faded, chipped, a bit of rust,
scuff decals and a dent). Haggle with sellers who have personalities,
inspect in person, or get sold a lemon. Engines are no longer sold at the
garage: haul one back on a trailer and the shop fits it for labour.
Trailers and groomers need the new hitch receiver. The Workshop tab
restores condition; the wear stays.

Real Estate: four depot cabins (two herder cabins, two new lakeside ones)
with weekly rent from tourists, upgrades, a fuel cache with a weekly bill
and arrears, summer lets through the summer skip, and the Map's Depots
layer. Scripts ?v=36.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P63TQRcpqHQKHbWoH9dUwo
